// two structs with no `operator ==` between them. the message is about the operands the author
// wrote, and it stays that way however many `==` declarations the program happens to link - the
// standard library declares two, for `string` and `string::view`, and neither belongs here
//
// this is the wording a use site had before any operator was declared anywhere. it lives in
// AST::binary_unsupported_operands so the built-in path and the operator-call path cannot drift

struct P { int32 $v; }

$a = P(1);
$b = P(2);

echo $a == $b;
